{"title":"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of the region defined by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality\" title=\"Inequality\">inequality</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b732c7132b14e1d2127007081a9af5e4c41c2e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|3x-18|+|2y+7|\\le3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fc0ec7234aa0ba2530edf248c3b29b2cee131af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 3\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{7}{2}\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 4\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"350\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We note that the area of a shape is invariant under translation, meaning that we can translate the inequality left <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units and up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea8d30f111d2f213c3486ec29afd22094d711beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> units without changing the area of the shape defined by the inequality. Doing this, we get a new inequality that is easier to work with:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a19f2f8dd7ca0806a76ba3bfc99a47c9ab449dbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|3x| + |2y|\\leq 3\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This forms a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rhombus\" title=\"Rhombus\">diamond</a> centered at the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Origin\" title=\"Origin\">origin</a> with vertices at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4caf927860c15ba28049dc7e26fe77f56b6ec52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\pm 1, 0), (0, \\pm 1.5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />. To calculate the area of this diamond, we can split it into four <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruence_(geometry)\" title=\"Congruence (geometry)\">congruent</a> right triangles. The area of each right triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02eb00201bb1cca99411af70f1ac6ab552480970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1\\cdot1.5}{2}=\\frac{1.5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />. Multiplying this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives us the area of the region defined by the inequality to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f701e8a155ce1da08edc48b8e0113059b038b581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot \\frac{1.5}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~ Danny Wang (ThePeeps191)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to the above solution, but instead we solve for the inequality.\n</p><p>In the first condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3c67646b9026576be5d3ad1311192bd93f2e18c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x - 18 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb38736093ffb9260d677782bd32c20e0e09e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c230b6bf35b03c7aa14068a3bc2372f74c8698f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y + 7 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfab3d5a74c22941772818f259138f4f7ddfcab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\geq -\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />.\nThen, the inequality becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd466fe86a54fe12f9ebd6b882092479c3120ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x - 18 + 2y + 7 \\leq 3\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4bb34e95fb3d33e2f431b3a977c5656e83555e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x + 2y - 11 \\leq 3\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adcb565240d7dcfdd2c920797d5325880da44f71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x + 2y \\leq 14\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9732628fa8ff387b63af7dbc10e923fab6c1afe0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y \\leq -\\frac{3}{2}x + 7\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />\nAlong with the constraint that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb38736093ffb9260d677782bd32c20e0e09e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfab3d5a74c22941772818f259138f4f7ddfcab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\geq -\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />, we have a segment of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52e53c61cf57ef1e41a56ca9ae842a5b849c5c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -\\frac{3}{2}x + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" /> with endpoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5ac00999497834ee2c455764662786a31d7a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, -2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d7bb375bc6625aed8a757c617bb2144f0fdbe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7, -\\frac{7}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>In the second condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3c67646b9026576be5d3ad1311192bd93f2e18c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x - 18 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb38736093ffb9260d677782bd32c20e0e09e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c621061009e838720fb50e735f7ff60f28eccab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y + 7 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe6827d2f0c39f8e6526b06fec5c364362cff80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &lt; -\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />.\nThen, the inequality becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782edac0896ae75d386af671d0812934ca733ee8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x - 18 - 2y - 7 \\le 3\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796c973df42c7675fb0b8bcce252129cfbbf005a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x - 2y - 25 \\le 3\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71fffd01cbffef7f0913e0139b7546f979bd6b81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x - 2y \\le 28\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0cb65bb061ae5fef06a01e2714588e24639fb34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-2y \\le -3x + 28\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96480ef4151dc0a9f8f207e6708475fd769d9f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y \\geq \\frac{3}{2}x - 14\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" />\nAlong with the constraint that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb38736093ffb9260d677782bd32c20e0e09e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe6827d2f0c39f8e6526b06fec5c364362cff80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &lt; -\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />, we have a segment of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b9300d083c89bfbe931e290aeb1bb5cd77bf1c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" /> with endpoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58fef702cf177d63695b99dac7ec39a3c9d4203a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, -5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d7bb375bc6625aed8a757c617bb2144f0fdbe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7, -\\frac{7}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>In the third condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ad982085a3fcf9746350e3197501434016648a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x - 18 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/39199288426ebe55ad525db2669cbad6febc06aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/2/1c230b6bf35b03c7aa14068a3bc2372f74c8698f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y + 7 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfab3d5a74c22941772818f259138f4f7ddfcab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\geq -\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />.\nThen, the inequality becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34bafee04e234eafd19969b8089bd42f7b490897.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-3x + 18 + 2y + 7 \\leq 3\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17d2ef7d79a60d68c5b8e3cb0f76103bca4c2cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-3x + 2y + 25 \\leq 3\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1eee1df7c9bb074c938ae16f1da12cbc0687bd5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-3x + 2y \\leq -22\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/48165ca61f9e80360e958ee122a82a792bb00d80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2y \\leq 3x - 22\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3cec1f4ca166ea4d161902c0550938d247d499e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y \\leq \\frac{3}{2}x - 11\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />\nAlong with the constraint that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/39199288426ebe55ad525db2669cbad6febc06aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfab3d5a74c22941772818f259138f4f7ddfcab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\geq -\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />, we have a segment of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f55ff4c30bded6ec2cad9db11224910f40e24a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" /> with endpoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94ece5c55ba75fa6e114cde2aba2363fbc37985b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, -\\frac{7}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58fef702cf177d63695b99dac7ec39a3c9d4203a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, -5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We may of course still solve for the fourth segment, but it is obvious that the fourth segment would just be another line connecting the gap. Therefore, we see that the shape that is formed by this inequality is a rhombus. Since we know the length of the diagonals are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (by the endpoints of the previous solutions), we know that the area of the region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7191143601a427ff3a605bbc38d8cf6c23b8ea7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 = 3\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\nHence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ Kellan Zhang (ThePlenGuy)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A\">2008 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"